   "link": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7482796110957211650",
   "reposts": 1.0,
   "title": "Praxen 1.1 now reveals how your agent\u2019s risks connect.\n\nAI agent risks rarely fit neatly into one box.\n\nA prompt injection can become goal hijacking. Excessive agency can lead to tool misuse or unexpected code execution. These are not separate problems. They are connected views of the same underlying risk.\n\nPraxen now captures those connections.\n\nEach finding identifies both its primary OWASP risk and the related risks it also touches. Across the same 114 findings in our benchmark suite, Praxen increased related-risk mappings from 3 to 28 \u2014 more than 9\u00d7 as many connections from the exact same scans.\n\nYou can explore those relationships in a new heat map showing where model-level and agent-level risks overlap.\n\nAnd we did it without changing Praxen\u2019s detection or project maturity scoring. A fresh scan of all 12 benchmark agents reproduced every serious vulnerability with zero misses.\n\nSame trusted detection. A much clearer picture of risk.\n\nPraxen 1.1 is available now. Grab it free from GitHub.\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/gRrtY2CP",
   "views": 0.0
  },
